 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "How you move",
   "texto": [
    "**en**: **en bus**, **en train**, **en voiture** (by car), **en métro** is used for the means in which you travel within the vehicle. **à**: **à vélo** (on a bike), **à pied** (on foot) is used to go by bike or on foot. In the family speech you also hear **en vélo**; here we practice the recommended form in French care: **à vélo**.",
    "Above or without vehicle is used **à**: **à vélo** (on a bike), **à pied** (on foot).",
    "You can also say **Je prends le bus** (I take the bus).",
    "**Comment tu vas au travail ?** = how are you going to work?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "At the station",
   "texto": [
    "**Un billet pour Lyon** (a ticket to Lyon).",
    "**Aller simple** = one-way. **Aller-retour** = back and forth.",
    "**Le train part à quelle heure ?** (what time does the train leave?). It comes out of a **quai** (platform).",
    "For duration: **Ça dure combien de temps ?** (how long?). **Environ** = about."
   ]
